course: dictionary
lesson: 1490
title: Caution: care, a warning, or a verb
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Caution is a word with more than one meaning, so read the words around it. «Use caution when crossing the road» tells you to be very careful, not to avoid the road.
explain: A caution can also be a warning you can read. A sign saying «Caution: wet floor» tells you the floor may be slippery, so slow down. Here caution is a noun.
explain: «The famous stubbornness is really caution: on a rocky desert path, running blindly could mean a fall, so a donkey stops and thinks where a horse would bolt.» The donkey is not being stubborn for no reason. It is being careful to avoid danger. Swap in the word care and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Caution means great care to avoid danger or mistakes.
fact: A caution can also be a warning, like a sign saying «Caution: wet floor».
fact: In UK law, a caution is an official warning from the police instead of a charge.
fact: As a verb, to caution someone means to warn them to be careful, or not to do something again.
fact: Phrases: «with caution» means carefully; «err on the side of caution» means choose the safer option; «throw caution to the wind» means do something risky without worrying.
exercise: «Please use caution when crossing the road.» What does caution mean here? | A kind present | *Great care to avoid danger | A loud shout | A map of the road
exercise: On a sign that says «Caution: wet floor», what is caution? | A type of shoe | A kind of floor | *A warning | A game
exercise: «The teacher cautioned Sam not to run inside again.» What does cautioned mean? | *Warned him to be careful | Carried him home | Thanked him loudly | Gave him a prize
test: «Err on the side of caution» means: | *Choose the safer option | Take the biggest risk | Go faster | Forget about it
test: In UK law, a caution is: | A type of court case | A prize for good behaviour | *An official warning instead of a charge | A fine to pay at the shop
exam: The donkey in «The famous stubbornness is really caution» stops on the rocky path because it is: | Lazy | Thirsty | *Being careful to avoid a fall | Lost
